<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c7" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Restoration Shaman Trinkets in Phase 3</span></h2>We will once again want two raiding trinkets in Phase 3, which are much stronger than most alternatives, but starter or older phase geared characters can benefit from using some of the other trinkets listed below.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96757/horridons-last-gasp">
<img alt="Horridon's Last Gasp" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_eyeofthestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Horridon's Last Gasp</span></a> is a simple stat stick that grants you extra Mana passively, making it a strong trinket in all situations.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96933/lightning-imbued-chalice">
<img alt="Lightning-Imbued Chalice" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_mage_runeofpower.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightning-Imbued Chalice</span></a> provides a good throughput increase with its passive Intellect, and has an interesting effect that will cause additional healing passively as you accumulate Infinite Power charges from your regular healing.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94510/volatile-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Volatile Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_hunter_posthaste.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Volatile Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> is similar to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87175/essence-of-terror">
<img alt="Essence of Terror" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Essence of Terror</span></a> with higher item level, making it a fairly good trinket for Restoration Shamans.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94509/soothing-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Soothing Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_elemental_primal_life.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soothing Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> is bought from the same vendor, but provides extra Mana instead of throughput, making it less effective.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a> is still one of the best starting trinkets.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79330/relic-of-chi-ji">
<img alt="Relic of Chi-Ji" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_crane.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Chi-Ji</span></a> is another great option for starting characters.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87163/spirits-of-the-sun">
<img alt="Spirits of the Sun" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_drink_29_sunkissedwine.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spirits of the Sun</span></a> is still a strong stat stick that is easy to use.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87175/essence-of-terror">
<img alt="Essence of Terror" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Essence of Terror</span></a> is primarily a DPS trinket but can also be a decent trinket for healing as a Restoration Shaman.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=257881/thousand-year-pickled-egg">
<img alt="Thousand-Year Pickled Egg" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_egg_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thousand-Year Pickled Egg</span></a> procs from healing, and is fairly good for Restoration, being one of the best non-BiS trinkets for this phase if you can get its Haste proc at good times.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=257884/mithril-wristwatch">
<img alt="Mithril Wristwatch" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pocketwatch_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mithril Wristwatch</span></a> has passive Critical Strike, which is a good stat for Restoration, and your frequent damage spells will be able to activate it, making it a decent trinket if you are actively DPSing for Mana with <a class="q1 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=41536/glyph-of-telluric-currents">
<img alt="Glyph of Telluric Currents" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glyph_majorshaman.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Telluric Currents</span></a>.</div></li></ul>
